# R23 Rowan's Rise, the stone circle: the cult's welcome, the ring of fire as a puzzle (nine stones, four to break), the captives, the cult and its masks. Logic by hand.

~ arrive
cutscene wv_effigy_revealed
Narrator: The hill opens round you. Nine standing stones in a ring, runes burning orange along their edges, a bonfire at the heart. Chains run out of the rock to six figures kneeling at its foot.
cutscene wv_effigy_revealed_2
Narrator: Round them, dozens of dancers in animal masks sway to a hymn that has no words you can hold on to, and above the crown of the hill, against the huge moon, something very tall stands without moving.
cutscene end
set wv_stones_seen
quest wickers_vigil ring_of_fire
-> END

~ calm
Narrator: The runes along this stone burn steady and orange. The dancers' song seems to be what holds the fire back from the kneeling figures, for now.
-> END

~ welcome
Narrator: The nearest dancer, a baker's wife in a hare mask, turns from the hymn with her arms wide as if she had been waiting for you.
holly_aster [smile]: Friends! You have come to hear the song. It is not hard to learn. Come in, come in, and sing.
set wv_welcome_n += 1
-> welcome_menu

~ welcome_menu
if flag.wv_welcome_n >= 3
-> ring_lights
endif
* Play along and hum the tune -> welcome_hum
* Ask who the six are and why they are chained -> welcome_ask
* [Insight DC 14] Watch the dancers' faces for who is who -> welcome_see | welcome_blur
* Walk toward the stones while they sing -> welcome_walk
* Ask the dancers to unchain the captives -> welcome_demand
* Strike the nearest dancer down -> welcome_attack

~ welcome_hum
Narrator: They beam at you and sing louder. The hymn is warm, and the warmth is wrong, like a hand on the back of the neck.
set wv_welcome_n += 1
-> welcome_menu

~ welcome_ask
holly_aster [sly]: Those are the offering, dear. A gift. They will be glad of it, afterwards, when the Queen walks. Join us and you will be glad too.
set wv_welcome_n += 1
-> welcome_menu

~ welcome_see
Narrator: Under the masks, faces you know. The barber. The merchant. The painter. The deputy, with his hare's foot on a cord. The innkeeper, in a mask with its own antlers, singing with her eyes closed.
set wv_unmasked_seen
set wv_welcome_n += 1
-> welcome_menu

~ welcome_blur
Narrator: Masks, firelight, motion. You cannot tell one dancer from another, but a few of the voices in the hymn you have heard across a counter.
set wv_welcome_n += 1
-> welcome_menu

~ welcome_walk
Narrator: They part for you with delighted smiles. You walk among them to the rim of the circle before they think to ask why.
set wv_grace
-> ring_lights

~ welcome_demand
holly_aster [angry]: They are not ours to loose. Wait for the Queen.
Narrator: The song falters, a bar, two. The dancers' smiles hold, but their eyes have stopped being friendly.
-> ring_lights

~ welcome_attack
Narrator: The nearest dancer drops, still humming. The hymn does not stop. It rises.
-> ring_lights

~ ring_lights
set wv_welcome_done
set wv_ring_started
Narrator: Fire runs round the stones' edges, and a wall of it stands up from the ring, white at the core and red at the rim. It will burn anything that touches it, and the only way in or out now is through the hymn.
Narrator: The bonfire leans toward the kneeling captives, as a dog leans toward a hand. Four of the nine stones must go dark, or one captive a round will be given to it.
quest wickers_vigil ring_of_fire
-> END

~ holly
holly_aster [sad]: Keep my daughters out of this, and the Queen's name out of my mouth. I never wanted her to walk. I only wanted to see them grow.
Narrator: She tears the hare mask from her face. Her hands shake. She walks to the nearest stone and drives her shoulder into it, and the runes there gutter and go out.
set wv_stones_down += 1
set wv_stone_7_down
set cultist_holly_aster = "turned"
set cultist_holly_turned
set wv_holly_declined
-> END

~ stone_1
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 1
-> disable

~ stone_2
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 2
-> disable

~ stone_3
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 3
-> disable

~ stone_4
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 4
-> disable

~ stone_5
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 5
-> disable

~ stone_6
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 6
-> disable

~ stone_7
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 7
-> disable

~ stone_8
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 8
-> disable

~ stone_9
Narrator: Runes along the stone's face crawl and burn. Under them are the cult's chains, and under those, the shape of something that wants the fire to stay.
set wv_stone_cur = 9
-> disable

~ disable
* [Athletics DC 15] Wrench the runes off the face of it -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* [Sleight of Hand DC 15] Work the focus out of its socket -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* [Nature DC 15] Read the runes as a root and cut them -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* [Religion DC 15] Read the rite and speak the break -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* [Investigation DC 15] Find the one rune that holds the rest -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* [Arcana DC 15] Unravel the weave -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* [knows:dispel_magic] Cast Dispel Magic on the stone -> stone_ok
* [Athletics DC 17] Smash the stone outright (AC 17) -> stone_ok | stone_fail
* Step away -> END

~ stone_ok
Narrator: The runes shudder, gutter and go out. Heat leaves the stone like breath, and it stands grey and blind in the firelight.
set wv_stones_down += 1
if flag.wv_stone_cur == 1
set wv_stone_1_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 2
set wv_stone_2_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 3
set wv_stone_3_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 4
set wv_stone_4_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 5
set wv_stone_5_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 6
set wv_stone_6_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 7
set wv_stone_7_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 8
set wv_stone_8_down
elif flag.wv_stone_cur == 9
set wv_stone_9_down
endif
-> ring_tick

~ stone_fail
Narrator: A gout of flame bursts out of the stone at the one who touched it.
check Dexterity DC 17 -> stone_half | stone_full

~ stone_half
Narrator: You throw yourself aside and take only the edge of it.
damage 2d8 fire
-> ring_tick

~ stone_full
Narrator: The fire catches you full on, and the stone stays lit.
damage 5d8 fire
-> ring_tick

~ ring_tick
set wv_ring_round += 1
if flag.wv_stones_down >= 4
-> ring_fall
endif
if flag.wv_grace and flag.wv_ring_round <= 2
Narrator: The dancers are still singing at the edge of the ring and not yet looking. The bonfire does not throw this round.
-> END
endif
-> flame

~ flame
Narrator: The bonfire leans toward the chained captives and gathers itself into a gout. It is going for one of them. There is a heartbeat to do something about it.
* [Dexterity DC 17] Throw yourself in the way of the flame -> intercept | burn
* [Athletics DC 15] Heave the captive's chain out of the rock and haul them clear -> chain | burn
* Hold your ground at the stones; there is no reaching them -> burn

~ intercept
Narrator: You hit the flame shoulder first, and it breaks on you instead.
damage 4d8 fire
-> END

~ chain
Narrator: The chain parts in a spray of hot iron, and the captive is out from under the flame, coughing, and crawling away.
-> END

~ burn
if flag.wv_captives_lost == 0
Narrator: The flame takes Doris Squire in the chest. There is a shout, and a light, and a blue-green mote lifts off the stones and goes up the hill.
set vigil_burned_doris_squire
elif flag.wv_captives_lost == 1
Narrator: The flame takes Siv Harga in the chest. There is a shout, and a light, and a blue-green mote lifts off the stones and goes up the hill.
set vigil_burned_siv_harga
elif flag.wv_captives_lost == 2
Narrator: The flame takes Marianna Grey in the chest. There is a shout, and a light, and a blue-green mote lifts off the stones and goes up the hill.
set vigil_burned_marianna_grey
elif flag.wv_captives_lost == 3
Narrator: The flame takes Beatrice Wells in the chest. There is a shout, and a light, and a blue-green mote lifts off the stones and goes up the hill.
set vigil_burned_beatrice_wells
elif flag.wv_captives_lost == 4
Narrator: The flame takes Jean Myriel in the chest. There is a shout, and a light, and a blue-green mote lifts off the stones and goes up the hill.
set vigil_burned_jean_myriel
elif flag.wv_captives_lost == 5
Narrator: The flame takes Finneas Trout in the chest. There is a shout, and a light, and a blue-green mote lifts off the stones and goes up the hill.
set vigil_burned_finneas_trout
endif
set vigil_deaths += 1
set wv_captives_lost += 1
if flag.wv_captives_lost >= 6
Narrator: There is no one left to burn. The ring gutters.
-> ring_fall
endif
-> END

~ ring_fall
Narrator: The last rune goes dark, and the wall of fire folds in on itself. Silence, for a breath, where the hymn was. Then the sound of dancers drawing in air.
if not flag.vigil_burned_doris_squire
set vigil_saved_doris_squire
endif
if not flag.vigil_burned_siv_harga
set vigil_saved_siv_harga
endif
if not flag.vigil_burned_marianna_grey
set vigil_saved_marianna_grey
endif
if not flag.vigil_burned_beatrice_wells
set vigil_saved_beatrice_wells
endif
if not flag.vigil_burned_jean_myriel
set vigil_saved_jean_myriel
endif
if not flag.vigil_burned_finneas_trout
set vigil_saved_finneas_trout
endif
set wv_ring_down
-> cult_turns

~ cult_turns
Narrator: The dancers drop the hymn, and with it the smiles. Sickles come out of the straw. The baker, the deputy and the merchant draw close together, and the one called Howie lifts his mask like a man at the end of a long day.
set wv_cult_started
combat wv_cult

~ ring_fall_scene
Narrator: The ring is down, and the cult knows it.
-> cult_turns

~ captive
Narrator: A chained villager looks up at you with raw eyes.
* Tell them to hold on -> captive_hold
* Tell them what you have seen of the cult -> captive_tell
* Leave them -> END

~ captive_hold
Narrator: They nod, once, with their jaw clenched.
-> END

~ captive_tell
Narrator: You tell them the cult's faces. They do not look surprised, only tired.
-> END

~ captive_freed
if flag.vigil_saved_doris_squire and not flag.wv_doris_squire_thanked
Narrator: Doris Squire stands rubbing their wrists, and says a thing you will not forget.
set wv_doris_squire_thanked
elif flag.vigil_saved_siv_harga and not flag.wv_siv_harga_thanked
Narrator: Siv Harga stands rubbing their wrists, and says a thing you will not forget.
set wv_siv_harga_thanked
elif flag.vigil_saved_marianna_grey and not flag.wv_marianna_grey_thanked
Narrator: Marianna Grey stands rubbing their wrists, and says a thing you will not forget.
set wv_marianna_grey_thanked
elif flag.vigil_saved_beatrice_wells and not flag.wv_beatrice_wells_thanked
Narrator: Beatrice Wells stands rubbing their wrists, and says a thing you will not forget.
set wv_beatrice_wells_thanked
elif flag.vigil_saved_jean_myriel and not flag.wv_jean_myriel_thanked
Narrator: Jean Myriel stands rubbing their wrists, and says a thing you will not forget.
set wv_jean_myriel_thanked
elif flag.vigil_saved_finneas_trout and not flag.wv_finneas_trout_thanked
Narrator: Finneas Trout stands rubbing their wrists, and says a thing you will not forget.
set wv_finneas_trout_thanked
endif
-> END

~ aftermath
Narrator: The circle is quiet. The dancers who are not dead lie where they fell, masks off, faces slack. The baker sits against a stone with her daughters' names on her lips.
-> aftermath_menu

~ aftermath_menu
* Bind the living and leave them for the village to judge -> spare
* Finish what is left of the cult -> slay
* Take their masks and leave them to find their own way home -> unmask

~ spare
Narrator: You bind them with their own ribbons. The cult limps off at dawn, those that can, and the village will live with what it knows.
set cultist_alda_farnum = "spared"
set cultist_howie_butterman = "spared"
set cultist_gaston_doray = "spared"
set cultist_randall_graham = "spared"
set cultist_baltus_tolliver = "spared"
if not flag.cultist_holly_turned
set cultist_holly_aster = "spared"
endif
set wv_aftermath_done
standing old_ways +1
-> END

~ slay
Narrator: It is quick and ugly. The wicker above the hill waits through all of it.
set cultist_alda_farnum = "slain"
set cultist_howie_butterman = "slain"
set cultist_gaston_doray = "slain"
set cultist_randall_graham = "slain"
set cultist_baltus_tolliver = "slain"
if not flag.cultist_holly_turned
set cultist_holly_aster = "slain"
endif
set wv_aftermath_done
standing old_ways -2
-> END

~ unmask
Narrator: Without the masks, the cult is a few frightened villagers in stage clothes. They look at the fire on the hill and begin, very slowly, to leave.
set cultist_alda_farnum = "unmasked"
set cultist_howie_butterman = "unmasked"
set cultist_gaston_doray = "unmasked"
set cultist_randall_graham = "unmasked"
set cultist_baltus_tolliver = "unmasked"
if not flag.cultist_holly_turned
set cultist_holly_aster = "unmasked"
endif
set wv_aftermath_done
-> END

~ effigy
Narrator: On the crown of the hill, against the huge moon, it stands: a wicker man sixty feet tall, bound with wire and iron, its chest and limbs hollow cages. In the cages, people are standing very still.
set wv_effigy_seen
quest wickers_vigil shadow_of_the_wicker_man
-> END

~ fall_back
Narrator: The way back down is open. The village is a long road behind you, and the fire on the hill will not wait for it.
-> vigil/square:retreat_confirm

